Adapted from DeepTutor (original path -> this project):
  deeptutor/learning/mastery.py     -> scripts/mastery.py
  deeptutor/learning/scheduler.py   -> scripts/scheduler.py
  deeptutor/learning/models.py      -> scripts/ledger.py (evidence and error
                                       record fields, knowledge and error types)
  deeptutor/learning/prompts/en.yaml (explain, feynman, practice, error
                                       diagnosis prompts) -> skills/*/SKILL.md

Changes made: the code is rewritten in Python standard-library style
(pydantic models replaced by dataclasses), reduced to the parts this plugin
uses, and wired to an append-only event log. Prompts are reworded for Claude
Code skills. All reasoning is done by Claude; no other model API is called.

Further differences from DeepTutor:
  - scheduler: DeepTutor's seconds-based LEARNING_DEBUG switch, the Protocol and
    alias definitions, get_due_tasks, schedule_next and set_desired_retention are
    not ported; the retention target is fixed at 0.9.
  - mastery: scripts/ledger.py feeds compute_mastery with 1.0/0.5/0.0 per unaided
    attempt (hinted attempts are excluded), following deeptutor/learning/service.py.
  - KnowledgeType/ErrorType: the legacy value mappings are not ported, so old
    DeepTutor values are rejected.
  - error records: DeepTutor's status names (active, retrying, review, graduated)
    are kept, but graduation is stricter. DeepTutor graduates an error after one
    correct retry of the same question (deeptutor/learning/service.py); this
    project requires two consecutive correct answers, and a wrong or partial one
    in between resets the count.
  - skills/learn, skills/quiz, skills/review are derived in part from DeepTutor's
    prompts and each says so at the top.

Known limit inherited from DeepTutor: the retention scheduler is an
exponential-forgetting baseline with type-specific priors, not a calibrated
FSRS fit.
